Require a KLL image's retained count to agree with n.

A non-empty KLL sketch retains at least one item and no more than n, and
with a single level nothing was compacted, so n equals the number retained.
serialize() chooses the single-item layout by n == 1 while the buffer it
allocates is sized from the retained count, so an image breaking this made
it write past the buffer (heap-buffer-overflow WRITE, found by data.sketches
tools/fuzz). Checked in both overloads after the levels.

--- a/kll/include/kll_sketch_impl.hpp	2026-11-16 22:03:05
+++ b/kll/include/kll_sketch_impl.hpp	2026-11-16 22:03:05
@@ -486,6 +486,17 @@
   }
   levels[num_levels] = capacity;
   check_levels(levels);
+  // A non-empty sketch retains at least one item and no more than n, and
+  // with a single level nothing was compacted, so n is exactly the number
+  // retained. serialize() picks the single-item layout by n == 1 while the
+  // size it allocates is computed from the retained count, so an image that
+  // breaks this made it write past its buffer.
+  {
+    const uint32_t retained = levels[num_levels] - levels[0];
+    if (retained == 0 || retained > n || (num_levels == 1 && n != retained)) {
+      throw std::invalid_argument("Possible corruption: KLL item count inconsistent with n");
+    }
+  }
   optional<T> min_item;
   optional<T> max_item;
   if (!is_single_item) {
